WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.193 --> 00:00:02.303
- [Woman] Are you making a wish?

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.080
- Extra-Ordinary Birthdays
is an organization

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:06.840
that I created to instill self-worth

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.790
in homeless children on their birthday.

00:00:10.126 --> 00:00:11.000
(cheering and clapping)

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.978
When I started, some people
said, it's just a birthday.

00:00:14.978 --> 00:00:17.970
I mean, my god, they need
a house, they need this.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.784
I'm like yeah, they need
to be recognized too.

00:00:20.784 --> 00:00:23.451
(playful music)

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:29.030
I'm Schinnell Leake, and I'm the founder

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:30.610
of Extra-Ordinary Birthdays.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:32.920
We go and partner with shelters to provide

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.880
personalized birthday parties
for homeless children.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.570
I want every child to feel like

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.380
their parents ordered this party up.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.074
We're just the people that
are helping to make it happen.

00:00:43.074 --> 00:00:44.297
- This is her little dress.

00:00:44.297 --> 00:00:45.130
- Oh my.

00:00:46.039 --> 00:00:47.860
That says unicorn all day long.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:48.693
- Doesn't it?

00:00:48.693 --> 00:00:49.950
It's like super cute.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:53.460
- Since 2010 we have
celebrated over 800 kids.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:56.675
I started with one shelter and in 2011

00:00:56.675 --> 00:01:00.790
we got another shelter and we
are now up to nine shelters.

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:03.435
And that's in D.C.,
Maryland, and Virginia.

00:01:03.435 --> 00:01:05.768
(cheering)

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.710
Extra-Ordinary Birthdays is not just me.

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:13.360
We have our party planners.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.880
They are the heart and soul of EOB

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.180
because they are planning parties

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:18.880
for children they don't know.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:20.510
That is hard to do.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:23.109
Goody bags, oh my god.

00:01:23.109 --> 00:01:24.710
- Goody bags.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.520
- [Schinnell] Now that is over the top.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.020
And they're putting all of this together

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:31.090
from the plates to the
napkins, the tablecloths,

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.060
they are creating the center pieces.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:35.680
All of this will be part
of the efforts we doing

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:37.333
to transforming the shelter.

00:01:40.273 --> 00:01:42.070
(playful music)

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:45.070
One of my greatest joys
is their first response

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:46.770
when they come in the room.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:50.010
Their expectations are so
low that when they come in

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:52.914
they just can't believe this party.

00:01:52.914 --> 00:01:54.331
- [Woman] Cheese!

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.113
- [Schinnell] And we've hit it

00:01:56.113 --> 00:01:57.560
on the head every single time.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:00.000
So we have this questionnaire
that basically asks

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.080
the children's name,
their age, who's coming.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:04.270
We usually say to them,

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:06.420
give us three things on your wish list.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.590
Three things that they want.

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:09.780
- This is also part of her gift.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.150
I didn't bring her other gifts

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.540
but I will have them tomorrow.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.968
Because they were super huge.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.264
- Okay.

00:02:16.264 --> 00:02:18.931
(playful music)

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:24.404
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:02:24.404 --> 00:02:25.700
♪ Happy birthday ♪

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.463
- [Schinnell] And then we
always ask them what kinda cake.

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:31.330
- [Group] Yay!

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.720
- And how awesome is it

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:34.100
that we are able to fill that?

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:36.743
Because that's specifically
what that child wants.

00:02:39.998 --> 00:02:42.248
(laughter)

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:45.000
The people that come to the parties

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.840
are other children in the shelter.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.400
When a child is homeless,

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.620
they're not inviting
their friends from school.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:53.580
Their friends from school don't
know they live in a shelter.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.730
Their friends are in the shelter.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:59.320
So we really are too about
building this community.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.300
It's more about the birthday child,

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:04.050
but it's about the culture of those

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.880
other homeless children too.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.990
Because they're going away with goody bags

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:09.490
just like everyone else.

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:11.370
And these are things that are speaking

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:13.380
to them in quiet ways.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:16.780
Even though it's not their
birthday, we are still having

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:19.663
some type of impact on
that child for that moment.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:25.340
This mother said something
so profound to me.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:27.650
She says, when you are homeless,

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:29.813
the system reminds you of that every day.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:33.330
She said, my daughter did
something normal today.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:34.780
She went to a birthday party.

00:03:35.738 --> 00:03:38.120
- [Woman] Wow, cool purse.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:39.740
- [Schinnell] For that moment,

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.853
that mom was able to be a mom.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:47.070
So the children get to see
their parents as parents.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:49.460
And not in a line, getting food

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:52.150
or being part of the handout.

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:55.680
And that's what I love
because what I wanted to do

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:59.630
is to take the simple
concept of a birthday party

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:02.028
and disrupt everyone's thinking.

00:04:02.028 --> 00:04:04.695
(playful music)

